   "page": 87,
   "box": 0,
   "kind_hint": "outside",
   "section": null,
   "section_y": -1,
   "indent": 0,
   "parent": null,
   "text": "• Check for tick bite (small dark brown/black scab). If tick bite or tick present and headache, temperature ≥ 38°C or body pain, tick bite fever likely 38. • If unexplained rash or lesion/s of skin/genitals/anus/rectum/mouth/eyes and ≥ 1 of: headache/backache/body pain, swollen lymph nodes, temperature > 38.5°C, fatigue, sore throat/nasal congestion/ cough consider mpox 40. • If patient started any medication, such as an antiseizure medication, ART, TB medication, co-trimoxazole or TB preventive treatment (TPT) in the past 3 months, consider drug rash 88. • Test for syphilis 66 and HIV 124.",
   "bbox": [
